@startuml
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
skinparam noteTextAlignment left
' purpose: a finished or in-progress game that lives in localStorage can be exported as a file the player keeps
' status: proposed 2026-09-17, not implemented; _spec/_plans/ is exempt from the SPEC-reference rule.
' would touch: not in this tree — no localStorage game blob, export, or replay
'   types exist under the sandbox checkout (measured 2026-09-17). Locate the
'   owning persist module before a covers: line can be honest.
'   outcome this file must copy ........ _spec/_plans/forfeit-as-loss.puml
'   the draw bug it must be able to dump _spec/_plans/turn-45-draw-stop.puml
'   difficulty the blob should record .. _spec/_plans/chess-save-difficulty.puml
' Notes are capped at 5 lines x 50 columns; one idea per anchor.
'
' ── WHAT THE LINE ITEM SETTLES ─────────────────────────────────────────────
' "game export from localstorage" is a PORTABILITY gap. The live store is the
' browser's localStorage. The player needs a file they can keep, send, or
' attach to a bug. The store stays; the file is a copy, not a migrate-off.
'
' ── WHAT IT DOES NOT SETTLE ────────────────────────────────────────────────
'   import of that file (export-only is a valid first slice)
'   schema versioning and forward readers
'   whether a partial turn-45 dump is in scope for the first ship
'   PII: player names, tokens, anything that is not the board
'
' A dump that omits the outcome enum will fight forfeit-as-loss and the draw
' stop: the file will disagree with the screen. Export reads the same record
' the engine writes, or it is not an export.
title PLANNED — localStorage stays the live store;\nexport is a file copy of that record

database "localStorage\nlive game record" as LS <<db>>
component "export action" as EX <<app>>
component "**a file the player keeps**\nboard · clock · outcome · version" as FILE <<app>>
component "import (not required\nfor the first slice)" as IMP <<app>>
component "**a dump that disagrees**\nwith the screen" as LIE <<error>>

LS ARROW_MAIN EX
EX ARROW_MAIN FILE
FILE ARROW_OPTIONAL IMP
EX ARROW_ERROR LIE : if it rebuilds state\ninstead of copying it

note bottom of LS
  **The live localStorage store is not the export
  feature, because finished games already persist
  there between sessions.** Export serialises that
  blob rather than inventing a second save format
  that can drift.
end note

note bottom of FILE
  **Version the envelope, because an unversioned
  dump becomes unreadable the moment a field is
  renamed.** Wrap the record with a schema
  identifier so a later import can refuse rather
  than crash.
end note

note right of LIE
  **Copy the stored record rather than
  reconstructing the board by replaying historical
  moves.** Reconstruction will disagree the moment
  a rules patch lands, so persist exactly what was
  stored.
end note

legend bottom
  **The order to do it in**
  ==
  **1. Document the live blob.** Key name, JSON shape, which fields are the
  board, the clocks, the outcome, and the difficulty. No covers: line until
  that shape is copied from code, not guessed.
  --
  **2. Ship export as a download.** Same JSON, plus a schema version. Outcome
  must be the engine's enum (forfeit is a loss once that plan lands). Do not
  strip the turn-45 trace — that dump is how the draw bug gets a fixture.
  ==
  **3. Import is a second slice.** A reader that round-trips the file is
  worth doing after one real export has been used as a bug attachment.
  --
  **Left open**: filename; whether multiple slots export as a zip; stripping
  display names.
end legend
@enduml
